# The covered-six Thompson plane and its ambient placement

The source commutator [V,Lᵥ] equals [⟨z⟩,Lᵥ] and lies in the actual block
layer U(K). For a subgroup A of K/O₂(K), its fixed subgroup is constructed
in that layer with no additional quotient. Its binary fixed space is
identified literally, and binary dimension four gives vector dimension
two over F₄ in the explicit hexacode coordinates.

The source assembly constructs the actual four-group coming from J(Tᵥ)⁺,
its order, fixed dimension and Baumann-image identity. It also constructs the
compatible core-to-plus injection and proves both kernel assertions, deriving
the relative block and module-containment premises of that comparison.

Baumann heredity lifts normalizers through the entire plus kernel. This gives
the literal source normalizer-image equality and placement in Mᵥ, and applies
`source_line_invariant_of_placement` to the same source commutator. The final
adapter consumes the genuine flag/local configuration and earlier 13.6.6,
13.6.14 and 13.6.20 conclusions. The hexacode model remains explicit as allowed;
the separate invariant-E₄ obstruction and covered-six exclusion are not asserted.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004, printed
pp.926–932, especially 13.6.22 on p.932.
-/
